# Dogfood Task 2 · Audit Timeline Humanization · Draft Reply for Accountant Email

*two tiny field-notes items in one builder cycle · 1–2 commits*

---

## Why

Two unrelated polish items, both small, bundled together so the builder cycle isn't ceremony-heavy.

**(A) Audit timeline shows internal event names.** The right column on `/app/inbox` shows entries like `analyzed by · invoice extractor`, `pipeline failed · llm call`, `not supported yet`. Those are internal slugs leaking through `eventLabel()`'s naïve `_→space, :→·` replacement. A potential client reading this thinks "this is a developer log." It should read like a human-readable history: "AI analysis · invoice extractor", "Approved by user", "Document uploaded".

**(B) Draft Reply only renders for `client_request`.** The DraftReplyPanel mounts only when `selected.type === 'client_request'`. The accountant email in the demo set is type `accountant_request` and is exactly the kind of message a user would want a draft for ("the accountant is asking for missing documents — write me a polite reply"). The reply prompt in `email_reply_draft_v1.txt` is already generic ("drafting a business email reply for a Romanian SME"), no prompt change needed — just widen `applies_to` and the frontend gate.

Neither item changes data shape, schema, or analyzer protocol.

---

## Scope

```
IN     audit label map        apps/web/src/routes/app/inbox/+page.svelte
                                replace eventLabel()'s naïve replace with a small map for known event types
                                + a fallback humanizer for prefixed events (analyzed_by:<x> · analysis_failed:<x> · pipeline_failed:<x>)
                                map covers: uploaded · approved · ocr_required · not_supported_yet
                                prefixed: analyzed_by:<analyzer> → "AI analysis · <analyzer human label>"
                                          analysis_failed:<analyzer> → "Analysis failed · <analyzer human label>"
                                          pipeline_failed:<step> → "Pipeline error · <step>"
                                analyzer human labels: invoice_extractor → "Invoice extractor", classifier → "Classifier",
                                  summarizer → "Summarizer", contract_reviewer → "Contract reviewer",
                                  document_indexer → "Document indexer", draft_reply_generator → "Draft reply"

       draft for accountant   apps/api/app/analyzers/draft_reply_generator.py
                                applies_to = {"client_request", "accountant_request"}
                              apps/web/src/routes/app/inbox/+page.svelte
                                gate: selected.type === 'client_request' || selected.type === 'accountant_request'

OUT    new event types           do not invent new audit events · just relabel existing ones
       prompt rewrite            email_reply_draft_v1.txt is generic enough · do not edit
       schema change             no Document/AuditEvent column change
       analyzer rename           keep internal names · only the display string changes
       any other UX item         later codons cover deep-links · view-original · search/filter
```

---

## Acceptance

```
1  open /app/inbox · select any document with analysis events
   → audit timeline shows human-readable strings only
   → no underscores · no colons · no analyzer slug like "draft_reply_generator"
   → unknown event types still render readably (graceful fallback)

2  re-seed and approve a doc → "Approved by user" appears (not "approved")

3  select the accountant email (email_accountant_missing_docs_april.pdf)
   → DraftReplyPanel renders below the analysis panel
   → draft body is in Romanian (or matches detected_language)
   → human_review_required=true · no Send button (existing safeguard)

4  re-seed and check: draft_reply_generator now runs on accountant_request docs
   → analyzer_outputs.draft_reply_generator is populated for that doc

5  npm run check passes · no new svelte-check errors
   eval harness still passes (draft_reply fixture is on the apartment client_request — unchanged)
```

